<article class="env-lemma" id="08PY">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08PY">Lemma <span data-tag="08PY">92.5.3</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a Noetherian ring. Let $A \to B$ be a finite type ring map. Let $\pi $, $\underline{B}$ be as in (<a href="/tag/08PR" data-tag="08PR">92.4.0.1</a>). If $\mathcal{F}$ is an $\underline{B}$-module such that $\mathcal{F}(P, \alpha )$ is a finite $B$-module for all $\alpha : P = A[x_1, \ldots , x_ n] \to B$, then the cohomology modules of $L\pi _!(\mathcal{F})$ are finite $B$-modules. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/08PS" data-tag="08PS">92.4.1</a> and Proposition <a href="/tag/08PX" data-tag="08PX">92.5.2</a> we can compute $L\pi _!(\mathcal{F})$ by a complex constructed out of the values of $\mathcal{F}$ on finite type polynomial algebras. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>